Subject: Cantor Phase3 Topology Scanner Formation Consistency Evidence Reconciliation Pruning and Growth

Description: Records rejected surface area and controlled proof-support growth after semantic refinement and constraint reapplication. It prevents a formation-only authority repair from becoming a scanner implementation, acquisition schema, clock design, receipt issuer, physical fixture, or speculative protocol expansion.

& [DispositionIdentity] is exact
  + [disposition_uuid] is 98d3b7f7-35c2-4082-b11d-8c270e0776a8
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is f761e445-9961-4a1f-9adc-f973514fd542
  + [state] is pruning_complete_growth_bounded_unsigned

& [P01_ProductionImplementation] is pruned
  + no Rust module, public API, scanner adapter, traversal engine, or receipt constructor
  + reason: selected artifact class is formation authority only

& [P02_CargoAndWindowsSurface] is pruned
  + no dependency, feature, lockfile, windows-sys call, unsafe block, handle, pointer, constant mask, or ABI change
  + reason: M2C remains separately source-selected and unsigned

& [P03_AcquisitionRuntimeForm] is deferred
  + no acquisition struct, producer identifier type, start field, completion field, traversal result type, or persistence record
  + reason: formation defines semantic edges; runtime representation belongs to later M2C source

& [P04_ClockAndTimestampDesign] is deferred
  + no wall clock, monotonic clock, tick type, duration, clock-domain identifier, read function, or comparison API
  + reason: exact causal order can be formed abstractly without activating time observation

& [P05_IssuerImplementation] is pruned
  + no output-only receipt wrapper, issuer key, signer, constructor, content-addressing change, or issuance entry point
  + reason: formation describes future issuer obligations but grants no issuer authority

& [P06_ConsumerAndLedger] is pruned
  + no receipt ledger, freshness clock, uniqueness state, single-use state, work-packet conversion, admission, or mutation authorization
  + reason: consumption remains M2E or later

& [P07_PhysicalFixtureAndExecution] is pruned
  + no T, S, W, P, I, A, R, E, or V fixture, disposable root, scan, canary, cleanup, or evidence capture
  + reason: physical plan remains designed_not_authorized_to_execute

& [P08_ScannerProfileRevision] is pruned
  + no scanner profile 0.2 and no traversal behavior change
  + reason: current discrepancy is evidence and receipt formation meaning, while observation policy stays 0.1

& [P09_UnrelatedFormationRewrite] is pruned
  + no cleanup or rewording of no-follow, identity, stream, attribute, Git, resource, fault, platform, or stage-gate clauses
  + reason: exact inheritance minimizes supersession and rollback scope

& [P10_LegacyMigration] is pruned
  + no conversion of quiescent_double_inventory or consistency to current meaning
  + reason: historical authority stays immutable and current governance changes prospectively

& [P11_BareDigestEvidence] is pruned
  + no acquisition or evidence carrier made from digest strings alone
  + reason: complete independent lineage is mandatory

& [P12_ReconciliationConversion] is pruned
  + no From, Into, builder, or inference edge from supplied Equal to NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + reason: Equal is necessary but acquisition, order, completeness, and scope remain independent

& [P13_StrongerEvidenceGrades] is deferred
  + no quiescent, stable, unchanged, supervisor-exclusive, transactional, immutable, or snapshot receipt formation
  + reason: their producers, provenance, enforcement, and consumers are not designed

& [P14_DistributedAndAcceleratedExecution] is pruned
  + no model, neural routing, shared inference, distributed participant, database mutation, or FPGA surface
  + reason: unrelated and explicitly locked

& [G01_ExactSupersessionTable] is accepted bounded growth
  + later canonical identifies prior signature, revised clauses, inherited clauses, and zero implementation authority
  + reason: formation lineage must be inspectable rather than implicit

& [G02_RoleCapabilityMatrix] is accepted bounded growth
  + formation, SJS processor, future acquirer, repeater, pure derivation, validator, issuer, and consumer roles are disjoint
  + reason: most semantic inflation routes are authority-role collapse

& [G03_AcquisitionRelationSchema] is accepted as conceptual growth
  + two identities, two complete lineage roles, one causal order, one common scope relation, and one subordinate reconciliation relation
  + reason: exact cardinality is necessary to state the future proof without runtime fields

& [G04_ForbiddenInferenceGraph] is accepted bounded growth
  + explicit negative edges block supplied-to-observed, left-right-to-temporal, Equal-to-acquisition, form-to-issuer, and evidence-to-world-state promotion
  + reason: prose nonclaims need machine-inspectable canonical counterparts

& [G05_InheritanceMatrix] is accepted bounded growth
  + later canonical enumerates unchanged scanner formation families rather than restating or silently dropping them
  + reason: narrow supersession must prove preserved obligations

& [G06_StaticGovernanceProof] is accepted bounded growth
  + repository checks prove old formation remains byte preserved, new canonical is separate, source hashes match, and production/Cargo deltas are zero
  + reason: this slice closes authority records, not runtime behavior

& [G07_RecursiveEvidenceMaintenance] is accepted bounded growth
  + current evidence manifests are rehashed only where governance artifacts they already bind change
  + reason: current clone-portable evidence must remain internally consistent without rewriting frozen history

& [GrowthBudget] is exact
  + new production modules zero
  + changed production modules zero
  + new dependencies zero
  + new public runtime types zero
  + new effect entry points zero
  + new executable profiles zero
  + one replacement formation signature candidate
  + ten requirements, twenty-four constraints, and bounded conceptual relation tables only

& [DispositionDecision] is passed
  + selected formation repair remains smaller than the runtime problem it describes
  + every deferred operational item requires new source and authority
  + no pruned item may reappear in later SJS artifacts without source revision
  + implementation authority is absent
  + execution authority is absent
  + physical authority is absent
